// SUBJECT NOTE — Frontier & Philosophy:
//   - Serious, respectful, accurate engagement with major Eastern philosophical traditions:
//     Buddhism/Zen (impermanence, non-self, suffering & its cessation, direct experience),
//     Vedanta/Advaita (Atman/Brahman, the self behind the self), and Taoism (the Tao, wu wei,
//     harmony with nature, the limits of language). Builds on L01 (the Buddhist "no fixed
//     essence" voice appeared there) and L04/L11.
//   - ACCURACY & RESPECT (calibration-critical): present these as rigorous philosophy in their
//     own right, NOT as mystical decoration or a self-help aesthetic. Avoid exoticizing,
//     flattening them into one "Eastern blob," or implying they're interchangeable — they
//     genuinely differ and even disagree. Use correct terms lightly and explain them.
//   - PROTECTIVE BACKBONE (essential): two-sided. (1) Take genuine wisdom seriously — these
//     traditions contain real, tested insight about mind, suffering, and living well, some of it
//     now echoed by psychology. (2) BUT "ancient" and "Eastern" do NOT mean "automatically true,"
//     and a huge commercialized "wellness/spirituality" industry sells distorted, cherry-picked,
//     or invented versions for profit. The mature stance: deep appreciation AND clear thinking —
//     you can draw real value from a tradition without checking your brain at the door or
//     accepting every supernatural claim as proven fact. Honor the user's own consciousness/
//     manifestation interests by modeling exactly this balance.
//   - EVENHANDED: don't rank East vs. West; present them as different toolkits asking sometimes-
//     different questions. Honesty tiers 2-4 (some claims tier-3 positions, some tier-4 mystery).
//   - Em-dashes natural; do NOT run em-dash replacement on Frontier files.
//
// Interaction format: PERSPECTIVES (screen 7) — content match for comparing traditions. Matches
// <Perspectives />: {id,type,headline,intro,perspectives:[{id,voice,era,stance,quote,argument,
// evidence,strengths_and_limits}],synthesisPrompt,reflectionPrompt}. 5 voices.
//
// QUIZ STANDARD (locked): 8 MC + 1 TF + 1 inference. Short ~1-line options, comparable length,
// plausible misconception distractors, correct rotated/not-longest; teaching in `explanation`.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

